From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:03:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: build the SAND program at draw time, report
 SAND failures

Three corrections to the host-sand path.

The NV12 program was built only at import time, and only the variant
(external SAND or plain 2D) of the buffer being imported. One queue can
hold both kinds of buffers, because host-sand falls back to NV12 when
the codec refuses SAND. So gpu_draw_nv12() now builds the program the
buffer needs before it draws and returns -EIO if it cannot.

When the GPU import of a SAND frame fails, the GPU path is turned off
for the queue, and nothing else can read SAND. Every later frame is then
dropped. Report that with error_report(), giving the error and the
column height and telling the user to turn host-sand off, instead of
only a diagnostic log line.

A failing S_FMT/TRY_FMT ioctl may rewrite the format struct. The NV12
retry now restores the format that was first sent before it changes the
pixel format, and it decides whether to retry from that saved copy
rather than from what the driver left behind.

No new switch. This only matters with host-sand on (default off).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [fix-up of this layer's host-sand patch]
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c |  9 +++++++++
 hw/virtio/virtio-media.c       | 14 +++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c
index b640c68de..0caf7f4f0 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c
@@ -601,6 +601,15 @@ static int gpu_draw_nv12(VirtIOMediaGpuBuf *b, GLuint dst_tex)
     glDisable(GL_DEPTH_TEST);
     glColorMask(GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE, GL_TRUE);
     glViewport(0, 0, b->width, b->height);
+    /*
+     * The program this buffer needs, built on first use: a queue can switch between SAND and
+     * linear NV12 (host-sand falls back when the codec refuses), and import only built the
+     * program of the buffer it imported.
+     */
+    if (!gpu_build_nv12_program(b->sand)) {
+        glBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
+        return -EIO;
+    }
     {
         GLenum target = b->sand ? GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES : GL_TEXTURE_2D;
 
diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c
index 9af507712..48971cd50 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-media.c
@@ -800,6 +800,15 @@ static void virtio_media_host_readable_body(void *opaque)
                                     qemu_log("virtio-media-diag: gpu_xfer: "
                                              "import failed (%d), GPU path "
                                              "off for this queue\n", e);
+                                    if (q->sand) {
+                                        /* Nothing else can read SAND: say so loudly. */
+                                        error_report("virtio-media: host-sand: GPU "
+                                                     "import of a SAND frame failed "
+                                                     "(%d, column height %u); every "
+                                                     "frame of this queue is now "
+                                                     "dropped -- turn host-sand off",
+                                                     e, q->sand_col_height);
+                                    }
                                 }
                             }
                         }
@@ -1692,13 +1701,16 @@ static int virtio_media_passthrough(VirtIOMediaSession *s, unsigned long code,
                 }
             }
         }
+        /* What the first attempt sends: a failing S_FMT/TRY_FMT may rewrite fields. */
+        struct v4l2_format sent = *f;
         int fmt_rc = ioctl(s->fd, code, payload);
 
         if (fmt_rc < 0 && want_rgba && code != VIDIOC_G_FMT &&
-            virtio_media_fmt_pixelformat(f) == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128) {
+            virtio_media_fmt_pixelformat(&sent) == V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128) {
             /* host-sand: the codec does not do SAND here; plain host-nv12 instead. */
             warn_report_once("virtio-media: host-sand: codec refused NV12_COL128, "
                              "using NV12");
+            *f = sent;
             virtio_media_fmt_set_pixelformat(f, V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12);
             fmt_rc = ioctl(s->fd, code, payload);
         }
